    "Description": "FRRouting is free software that manages TCP/IP based routing protocols. It supports BGP4, OSPFv2, OSPFv3, ISIS, RIP, RIPng, PIM, NHRP, PBR, EIGRP and BFD. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* frr: FRRouting: Denial of Service via crafted BGP UPDATE message (CVE-2026-37460)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Zebra is not installing the route in the kernel after flapping one of the physical link on the ocp worker node. [rhel-9.8.z] (JIRA:RHEL-152300)\n\n* frr triggers SELinux denials when reading root's Python site-packages directory on RHEL-9 (JIRA:RHEL-176258)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
